{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421956-character-creation-scion-2e","id":1421956,"title":"Character Creation Scion 2E","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-11-05T01:28:59-08:00","id":1421956,"title":"Character Creation Scion 2E","content":"I\u2019m starting the <b>Scion</b> 2E game \u2013 and found character creation rules a bit confusing. Even with added sum-up material of <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/313847/Scion-Character-Creation-Quick-Reference\" target=\"_blank\">Scion Character Creation Quick Reference</a> </b>( <b>SCCQR</b> in short ), I still have questions on it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Origin Tier</b></span><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Legend - Origin character get or not get Legend 1 score?</b> I thought that at <b>Origin</b> tier, characters are \u2018mortal\u2019, so they DO NOT have Legend \u2013 i.e. they have Legend 0 \u2013 however <b>SCCQR </b>point they get Legend 1. Who is right?</li> <li><b>Knacks \u2013</b> <b>As I understand, Origin characters get at start 1 Calling \u2013 and from that Calling list, they choose ONLY ONE Knack option for start. </b>So if I choose <i>Creator</i> as Calling, I can choose 1 Knack between <i>Innate Toolkit</i>, <i>Perfect Rendition</i>, <i>Reverse Engineer, Flawlessly Platonic</i> <i>Ideal, The Unlimited Quatermaster</i>, <i>We Go All Night </i>OR <i>Wireless Interface</i>. I get it right?</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-05-2020, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T01:39:41-08:00","id":1421959,"title":"","content":"Hi,<br /> <br /> on the matter of callings. Origin Characters get one Calling (with one dot) and one heroic knack. Later on in the finishing touches they may choose two additional Heroic Knacks. But even then they can only have one at the time active.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26520-mugbearer23","name":"Mugbearer23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T05:55:35-08:00","id":1421988,"title":"","content":"Origin level characters do not have Legend. Look at all the ready made characters in the Origin book. Also, in Hero it says when upgrading after the Visitation, you note your one dot of Legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T06:25:00-08:00","id":1422001,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar702_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"702\" data-vbnamecard=\"702\">ElfSpeaker</a>, you should corect the Legend error on Origin tier in <b>SCCQR.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T07:01:39-08:00","id":1422015,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the @. I\u2019ll get it corrected shortly","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my RPG podcast: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told</a><br /> Follow my ongoing Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"https://thefallofjiara.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log\" target=\"_blank\">The Fall of Jiara</a><br /> Check out my Community Content: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Chazz%20Kellner\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....hazz%20Kellner</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker","name":"ElfSpeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar702_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T07:26:25-08:00","id":1422024,"title":"","content":"<b>3. Callings - As I understand, at Origin tier, characters CANNOT take more Callings than one only?</b> If I choose Guardian, on <b>Origin</b> itself, I cannot take other Calling to mix-and-match Knacks from various lists? <b>Origin </b>book do not point that you can buy new Callings from Experiance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T07:29:16-08:00","id":1422026,"title":"","content":"Correct. At Origin, your character has one Calling and one active Knack from either that Calling or the General Knack list. Callings cannot be bought with experience (ever). Knacks can be bought with experience, but the number of active Knacks you can have is fixed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T08:59:26-08:00","id":1422042,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you don't buy Calling dots with XP. You get them as your Legend goes up.<br /> <br /> You gain 4 Calling Dots when your Legend increases to 1, after your Visitation (5 total Calling dots), and then you gain 1 more every even Legend dot.<br /> <br /> So at Legend 2 you have 6 total Calling Dots, at Legend 4 you have 7 dots, and so on.<br /> <br /> Edit: And to predict a future question: You can't just pay XP to switch your established Callings. At Hero Tier, you undergo what's called a Failure Deed or a Crisis to weaken your ties to a specific Calling (such as failing to slay a powerful foe for your Warrior Calling, or utterly break a heart as a Lover) and then can take up an Adoption Deed to gain a new Calling.<br /> <br /> At Demigod tier, there's a phase of the Ascension Path called the Threshold wherein you can more freely swap your Callings every session as you explore your personal Legend and play with your identities. Like my hypothetical Loki Scion Demigod may stop being a con artist for a bit and work with law enforcement to help bring in other criminals, losing her Liminal Calling and taking the Judge Calling as she experiments with being a force for justice. Then she tosses it aside because she reaffirmed that the law is often bullshit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 11-05-2020, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T09:33:24-08:00","id":1422055,"title":"","content":"<b>4. Skills - I get it right that in <i>Origin</i>, characters only get 18 Skill dots?</b> 9 from Primary Path, 6 from Secondary Path and 3 from Tertiary Path? In <b>SCCQR </b>there is also mentioned 5 extra free Skills dots - but I do not see rules for them in <b>Origin</b> book chapter...<br /> <br /> EDIT: No, <b>final sum is 23 Skill dots</b>, with 18 from Paths and 5 free later on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-14-2020, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T09:38:18-08:00","id":1422057,"title":"","content":"The Five Extra Skill Dots are mentioned in the Finishing Touches part of Character Creation in Origin. Page 98, under the heading &quot;Step Six: Finishing Touches&quot;. Right next to the extra Attribute Dot, and a choice of either two extra Knacks or four Birthright Dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T15:48:23-08:00","id":1422314,"title":"","content":"5. <b>Extra Knacks or Birthrights</b> - I suspect that line 'Add two heroic Knacks OR four points of Birthrights, see Scion: Hero...' is wrong on 'heroic' kind of Knacks for <b>Origin</b> tier?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-06-2020, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T16:39:18-08:00","id":1422326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421956-character-creation-scion-2e?p=1422314#post1422314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5. <b>Extra Knacks or Birthrights</b> - I suspect that line 'Add two heroic Knacks OR four points of Birthrights, see Scion: Hero...' is wrong on 'heroic' kind of Knacks for <b>Origin</b> tier?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. A little confusingly, Heroic Knacks are Knacks that take up only one active Knack &quot;slot.&quot; There are also Immortal Knacks in Hero, which take up two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T16:57:02-08:00","id":1422329,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it\u2019s confusing but correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my RPG podcast: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told</a><br /> Follow my ongoing Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"https://thefallofjiara.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log\" target=\"_blank\">The Fall of Jiara</a><br /> Check out my Community Content: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Chazz%20Kellner\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....hazz%20Kellner</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker","name":"ElfSpeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar702_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T17:00:11-08:00","id":1422330,"title":"","content":"I would let my players take two bonus Knacks of Heroic or Immortal type at Chargen... But I'd warn the players that if they're at Origin tier they shouldn't take Immortal Knacks because they won't be able to use them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T23:01:17-08:00","id":1422386,"title":"","content":"6.<b> So 'first chosen Knack' from Calling at <i>Origin</i> tier is also Heroic Knack?</b> Or Heroic Knacks ar only in <b>Hero</b> book and two alternative to Birghtrights are OTHER kind than those from <b>Origin</b> book? \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T04:56:45-08:00","id":1422410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421956-character-creation-scion-2e?p=1422386#post1422386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6.<b> So 'first chosen Knack' from Calling at <i>Origin</i> tier is also Heroic Knack?</b> Or Heroic Knacks ar only in <b>Hero</b> book and two alternative to Birghtrights are OTHER kind than those from <b>Origin</b> book? \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Heroic Knacks appear in both Origin and Hero and are the ones available to Origin characters. Origina characters can take two of these during the final touches.<br /> <br /> mmortal knacks are only available to Hero-tier and above. For character creation purposes, they &quot;cost&quot; two knacks relative to the Heroic Knacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my RPG podcast: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told</a><br /> Follow my ongoing Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"https://thefallofjiara.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log\" target=\"_blank\">The Fall of Jiara</a><br /> Check out my Community Content: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Chazz%20Kellner\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....hazz%20Kellner</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker","name":"ElfSpeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar702_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T05:05:03-08:00","id":1422411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421956-character-creation-scion-2e?p=1422386#post1422386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6.<b> So 'first chosen Knack' from Calling at <i>Origin</i> tier is also Heroic Knack?</b> Or Heroic Knacks ar only in <b>Hero</b> book and two alternative to Birghtrights are OTHER kind than those from <b>Origin</b> book? \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not quite sure what you're asking. Tell me if this helps:<br /> <br /> 1. At Origin, your character gets 1 Knack (from the Origin book). Choose it from the general Knack list or the one for your Calling.<br /> 1a. If the effect of the Knack mentions your Calling dots, you are assumed to have 1 dot in your Calling.<br /> 2. You can add 2 more Knacks in the Finishing Touches part of character creation (Origin, p.98), but remember that you can only have 1 active at a time (i.e., during a session).<br /> 3. You can later spend 10 XP to buy another Knack (still from the Origin book), but can still only have 1 active at a time.<br /> 3a. You cannot buy Immortal Knacks (from the Hero book) yet, because they require you to have 2 dots in a Calling. (Hero, p.183)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T06:16:05-08:00","id":1422422,"title":"","content":"Thanks, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"369\" data-vbnamecard=\"369\">Geoffrey</a> , it really clears Knacks issues. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>7. Are Virtues mandatory on <i>Origin</i> tier?</b> If yes, what do they add to the game? Can characters change Virtues of their Pantheon to other, unique to character?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-07-2020, 09:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T06:45:51-08:00","id":1422423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421956-character-creation-scion-2e?p=1422422#post1422422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"369\" data-vbnamecard=\"369\">Geoffrey</a> , it really clears Knacks issues. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>7. Are Virtues mandatory on <i>Origin</i> tier?</b> If yes, what do they add to the game? Can characters change Virtues of their Pantheon to other, unique to character?</div> </div> </div> </div>Origin pre-Visitation Scions do not get Virtues. They manifest post-Visitatiom. As for what they do, I made a post about them, give me time to track it down and i'll link it<br /> <br /> But Virtues are intended to be associated with Pantheons. Though if you break away from your Pantheon entirely you could possibly gain separate Virtues.<br /> <br /> Edit: Okay here we go-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alright the bulk of the explanation is on page 162-163 of the Origin book, but I'll lay it out here.<br /> <br /> Every Pantheon has a pair of Virtues attributed to them. These are two values that often crop up in the stories of this Pantheon. This is demonstrated via your character having a five-point bar, with one Virtue at each end. Let's pick, oh, the Teotl Virtues (because I like the Teotl). The Teotl Virtues are Hunger, a desire for MORE, more Glory, more Prestige, more Wealth, more Power... And Sacrifice, the Virtue of granting something significant for something greater than yourself.<br /> <br /> So we'll have Ash, a DJ Scion of Xochipilli. She starts with her Virtue Bar centered, like so: <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b>Hunger</b> O O X O O <b>Sacrifice</b></div> <br /> Certain actions can resonate with one of these Virtues. If you take an action that does so (and you'll be declaring this to your GM most of the time), you can spend Momentum to enhance your roll. Doing so will grant you a bonus die for the Momentum you spend. This will also move you one step along the bar towards the end with that virtue.<br /> <br /> So let's say that Ash, in combat, decides to go for broke and instead of setting up an attack for an ally, she goes for the kill, for personal desire of having the killing blow. I, her player, argue that this kind of personal interest would resonate with Hunger. Let's assume the GM agrees, so I spend my Momentum to enhance the roll, and gain two dice for the one Momentum spent. I would then move the point for her Virtue Bar like so- <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b>Hunger </b>O X O O O <b>Sacrifice</b></div> <br /> With me so far? Good. Now, if say, Ash made a major action that resonated with Sacrifice (possibly by missing a major DJ gig to help her friends), I'd get the same benefit... But I'd nudge the point to the middle of the bar, since it resonates with Sacrifice. The marker also goes towards the middle of the bar if you make a very deliberate action that goes against the Virtue at the end. So if Ash were to deliberately turn down something of great personal value to her (say, a Relic being offered if she turns on her friends but she refuses), then the marker would go back to the middle.<br /> <br /> As for Virtuous... Well let's go back to Ash, and say that she did enough Hunger-aligned things to push her Virtue Bar all the way to one end. <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b>Hunger</b> X O O O O <b>Sacrifice</b></div> <br /> Right, so Ash has engaged the Virtuous Condition (detailed in a sidebar at the top of page 163) for Hunger. She is going to be <i>difficult</i>. When in the grips of the Virtuous Condition, you <i>cannot go against the Virtue</i>. Ash can't turn away something that furthers or speaks to her Desire for More. However, this has impressive benefits. See that line about how spending Momentum on an Action that resonates with a Virtue gets you a bonus die? The Virtuous Condition also gives a bonus die per point of Momentum you spend on a Virtue-aligned action.<br /> <br /> <i>Those stack</i>. If Ash is in her Hunger Virtuous Condition and spends Momentum on a Hungry Action, she gets <i>three dice per Momentum spent</i>.<br /> <br /> The Virtuous Condition also gives more Momentum if your Virtue Rage gets you or a friend in trouble.<br /> <br /> You end this Condition by acting in a way that embraces the opposite Virtue while not necessarily acting against the one you're in. Or using the Balm Fatebinding benefit, that can work too.<br /> <br /> Hope this helped. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 11-07-2020, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T10:58:38-08:00","id":1422623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421956-character-creation-scion-2e?p=1422423#post1422423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Origin pre-Visitation Scions do not get Virtues. They manifest post-Visitatiom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where in the Origins book is this said?<br /> <br /> Why are they on the Origin character sheet if they are not in the game?<br /> <br /> I don't mean to sound angry or annoyed, I'm just confused.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T13:13:50-08:00","id":1422649,"title":"","content":"Yeah that\u2019s something I\u2019m curious about too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T13:27:58-08:00","id":1422651,"title":"","content":"Hm i think the Saint Denizen use the virtues even at the Origin tier.<br /> So that may be why it was included in the character sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T14:20:20-08:00","id":1422660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421956-character-creation-scion-2e?p=1422651#post1422651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm i think the Saint Denizen use the virtues even at the Origin tier.<br /> So that may be why it was included in the character sheet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because while pre-Visitation Scions don't get Virtues, as noted, SAINTS do, even at Origin tier.<br /> <br /> IIRC, the Origin book talking about Virtues in the Saint section says that Saints and Heroes get Virtues. So that says to me that Origin-tier pre-Visitation Scions do not get Virtues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T20:53:29-08:00","id":1422690,"title":"","content":"I cannot find anything in the Origin book that explicitly or implicitly says that Origin characters do not have Virtues. On the contrary I read the sidebar on page 70 as saying explicitly that they do; it says that Scions and mortals known as Saints gain Virtues, and a pre-visitation Scion is still a Scion, right?<br /> <br /> On page 162 it says that Saints gain Virtues but I see nothing that implies that this is in contrast to Scions, just that Saints are mortals who get Virtues.<br /> <br /> Note that I did not read what the Hero book says about the matter, maybe it presents another picture.<br /> <br /> Besides, Origin is more interesting with Virtues anyway since they represent how even Origin-level characters are larger than life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","user":"Aristarkos","date":".  I mistakenly wrote Momentum instead of Virtues 11-08-2020, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T00:43:06-08:00","id":1422703,"title":"","content":"8. Do Virtues are optional? I.E. <b>Can character have other Virtues than his Pantheons ones?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T09:24:47-08:00","id":1422756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421956-character-creation-scion-2e?p=1422703#post1422703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">8. Do Virtues are optional? I.E. <b>Can character have other Virtues than his Pantheons ones?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>If you have a Pantheon you will inherit those Virtues. That's how it works.<br /> <br /> If you take the steps to break free of your Pantheon and remove yourself utterly, then you would gain your own Virtues","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T03:03:51-08:00","id":1428451,"title":"","content":"9. Having done some PC creations for few games,<b> I often see in character creations that starting Origin characters have 5 in particular Skill</b> - you only need to have Skill in your 1st and 2nd Path for that. My a bit problem is that 5 dot is 'world master / Olympics' level character - so it's a bit crash with starting Origin characters concepts. <b>Should you move those 5th dots to other Skills? Or leave them at 5, even if it breaks a game setting logic a bit?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T03:14:59-08:00","id":1428452,"title":"","content":"Not really. Origin level characters are the best among mortals, if you pick the heroic knacks they can have you will see some fantastical things, beyond human level, like metalworking without tools and killing people with paper clips, and they are not divine yet. Also, they attracted attention of the gods, if they are not their kids, that\u2019s not something you do if you are not good in more than a few things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T04:36:08-08:00","id":1428454,"title":"","content":"To echo the sentiment, even as an Origin level character, you're already exceptional. You <i>should </i>have skills that match you with world masters. Storypath in general focuses on characters with amazing skills from the get go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my RPG podcast: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told</a><br /> Follow my ongoing Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"https://thefallofjiara.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log\" target=\"_blank\">The Fall of Jiara</a><br /> Check out my Community Content: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Chazz%20Kellner\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....hazz%20Kellner</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker","name":"ElfSpeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar702_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T22:30:12-08:00","id":1428561,"title":"","content":"So I want to know if I have this right for Hero-tier characters:<br /> <br /> 1. Immortal Knacks cost 2 &quot;active&quot; knack slots in play.<br /> 2. Immortal Knacks cost 2 knack choices at character creation.<br /> 3. Immortal Knacks and Heroic Knacks both cost 5 xp.<br /> <br /> So you can buy a bunch of Immortal Knacks with XP if you want, but can't have as many active as you could Heroic Knacks.<br /> <br /> Do I have that right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T03:47:07-08:00","id":1428582,"title":"","content":"All Knacks are Knacks when buying them, in the char gen or when spending XP.<br /> Immortal knacks only count as 2 Heroic knacks when activating them, that\u2019s how I read it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T10:11:11-08:00","id":1428613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421956-character-creation-scion-2e?p=1428582#post1428582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All Knacks are Knacks when buying them, in the char gen or when spending XP.<br /> Immortal knacks only count as 2 Heroic knacks when activating them, that\u2019s how I read it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Really? Because it doesn't seem like it:<br /> <br /> &quot;For each Calling, choose a number of Heroic Knacks equal to the Calling\u2019s rating; while they can learn more, they may only have as many active as they have Calling dots. <b>Alternately, you may choose a single Immortal Knack instead of two Heroic Knacks for any Calling two dots or higher.</b> If your character is also a creature of Legend, they replace one Calling with one appropriate to their nature.&quot;<br /> <br /> This suggests to me that it costs two &quot;knack slots&quot; to buy an Immortal Knack at character generation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T12:43:45-08:00","id":1428638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421956-character-creation-scion-2e?p=1428613#post1428613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Really? Because it doesn't seem like it:<br /> <br /> &quot;For each Calling, choose a number of Heroic Knacks equal to the Calling\u2019s rating; while they can learn more, they may only have as many active as they have Calling dots. <b>Alternately, you may choose a single Immortal Knack instead of two Heroic Knacks for any Calling two dots or higher.</b> If your character is also a creature of Legend, they replace one Calling with one appropriate to their nature.&quot;<br /> <br /> This suggests to me that it costs two &quot;knack slots&quot; to buy an Immortal Knack at character generation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I read it as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T12:58:15-08:00","id":1428646,"title":"","content":"Same, but it appears when it comes to spending XP, all knacks cost the same. So, if you want an immortal knack, maybe wait until you can buy it in-game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T13:24:59-08:00","id":1428651,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the book definitley intends for Immortal Knacks to &quot;cost&quot; two Herioic Knacks at character creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my RPG podcast: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told</a><br /> Follow my ongoing Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"https://thefallofjiara.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log\" target=\"_blank\">The Fall of Jiara</a><br /> Check out my Community Content: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Chazz%20Kellner\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....hazz%20Kellner</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker","name":"ElfSpeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar702_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-05T05:59:52-08:00","id":1431154,"title":"","content":"10. Origin Tier creation - Am I reading it correctly here - <b>Beside 6/4/2 dots in Attributes, characters also gets +2 dots in <i>all </i>of his Favored Approach ones?</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Not the +2 dots to spread among Favored Approach Atributes - only +2 dots for 3 Attrubutes, i.e. +6 dots? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <i>'A player distributes two additional dots to each of the Attributes in his Favored Approach.'</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-05T06:18:51-08:00","id":1431157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421956-character-creation-scion-2e?p=1431154#post1431154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">10. Origin Tier creation - Am I reading it correctly here - <b>Beside 6/4/2 dots in Attributes, characters also gets +2 dots in <i>all </i>of his Favored Approach ones?</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Not the +2 dots to spread among Favored Approach Atributes - only +2 dots for 3 Attrubutes, i.e. +6 dots? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <i>'A player distributes two additional dots to each of the Attributes in his Favored Approach.'</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep, the favored approach gives an extra 6 dots of attributes. <br /> <br /> I suggest picking approach before assigning the 6/4/2 becuase if you don't do that, you're likely to exceed 5 dots then have to reassign them anyway.<br /> <br /> You get a lot of dots of attriburtes in Storypath, <i>and that's OK.</i> The way the rules work, it encourages you to mostly be rolling polls with a lot of dice. That's part of what's very different from Storyteller and Storytelling systems. The roll drama gets more into what complications do you buy off or not and what stunts do you purchase with excess successes. It's not stated in the book, but the design intention is for most rolls (outside of combat) to come with a complication or two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my RPG podcast: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told</a><br /> Follow my ongoing Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"https://thefallofjiara.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log\" target=\"_blank\">The Fall of Jiara</a><br /> Check out my Community Content: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Chazz%20Kellner\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....hazz%20Kellner</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker","name":"ElfSpeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar702_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-05T07:46:07-08:00","id":1431166,"title":"","content":"11. Origin Tier - <b>I</b><b><b>s </b>there a way for character to become better in combat <i>without</i> rising Close Combat skill and Attributes</b>? Like learning some Knacks or things I missed in book? Beside of character being of <i>Guardian</i> or similar Calling - as you can only have one Calling on Origin. In <b>CoD</b> you would take a Merit or two for that...<br /> <br /> I have NPC in mind that should not be overkiller in Skills or Attributes - but maybe could learn a trick or two, simply by expierance. But character is strictly Trickster Calling to begin with...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-05T08:15:08-08:00","id":1431169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421956-character-creation-scion-2e?p=1431166#post1431166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">11. Origin Tier - <b>I</b><b><b>s </b>there a way for character to become better in combat <i>without</i> rising Close Combat skill and Attributes</b>? Like learning some Knacks or things I missed in book? Beside of character being of <i>Guardian</i> or similar Calling - as you can only have one Calling on Origin. In <b>CoD</b> you would take a Merit or two for that...<br /> <br /> I have NPC in mind that should not be overkiller in Skills or Attributes - but maybe could learn a trick or two, simply by expierance. But character is strictly Trickster Calling to begin with...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Antagonists do not use the same creation rules a player characters. Take a look at the Qualities on page 146 of Origin and the Flares starting page 149. Dice pools are set by the Archetype (p. 145) instead of Skill + Attribute. It's a <i>lot </i>easier to set up antagonists this way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my RPG podcast: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told</a><br /> Follow my ongoing Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"https://thefallofjiara.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log\" target=\"_blank\">The Fall of Jiara</a><br /> Check out my Community Content: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Chazz%20Kellner\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....hazz%20Kellner</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker","name":"ElfSpeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar702_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-05T08:25:46-08:00","id":1431170,"title":"","content":"I agree with Elfspeaker about using the Antagonist rules. They're baller.<br /> <br /> If you're dead set on statting the character out like a PC and not already throwing around +3 enhancement on your attacks, you have a couple of options. First, you can try to figure out some specialties which would be applicable to close combat attacks. Maybe your Larceny specialty of Misdirection or Sleight of Hand is used with deceptive movements to hide your true attack. Also, bring friends. Even if they don't attack, they can use Teamwork (pg. 65) to have them give enhancements to the main attacker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-05T08:51:22-08:00","id":1431175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421956-character-creation-scion-2e?p=1431166#post1431166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">11. Origin Tier - <b>I</b><b><b>s </b>there a way for character to become better in combat <i>without</i> rising Close Combat skill and Attributes</b>? Like learning some Knacks or things I missed in book? Beside of character being of <i>Guardian</i> or similar Calling - as you can only have one Calling on Origin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Scion is pretty focused in the legend growth and not much in the horizontal development of the character (this \u201csmall details\u201d drop to insignificant when you add scale as often as Scion can do). If the idea is to play only Origin tier you could import the Edges from TC and DRE, or trademarks from TCF and allow characters to use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-05T09:10:38-08:00","id":1431177,"title":"","content":"Antagonist is one, main enemy of this chronicle - that is also secretly ( to him ) another Scion. Book pointed to stat those as normal characters, so I stat him as normal Scion character. <b>Will look into</b> Specializations and maybe some Equipment Enhancments then. MAYBE will steal one or two Egdes, specificlly for him, if wil have time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-10-2021, 05:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-05T09:35:14-08:00","id":1431180,"title":"","content":"You could also create your own Trickster knacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-05T09:36:58-08:00","id":1431181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421956-character-creation-scion-2e?p=1431177#post1431177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Antagonist is one, main enemy of this chronicle - that is also secretly ( to him ) another Scion. Book pointed to stat thos as normal characters, so I stat him as normal Scion character. <b>Will look into</b> Specializations and maybe some Equipment Enhancments then. MAYBE will still one or two Egdes, specificlly for him, if wil have time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Per the examples in Titanomachy, you can definitely stat Scions uses the antagonist rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my RPG podcast: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told</a><br /> Follow my ongoing Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"https://thefallofjiara.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log\" target=\"_blank\">The Fall of Jiara</a><br /> Check out my Community Content: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Chazz%20Kellner\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....hazz%20Kellner</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker","name":"ElfSpeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar702_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T02:27:00-08:00","id":1431662,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Moving question to next page of topic, for ease.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-10-2021, 08:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T04:06:00-08:00","id":1431672,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that you shouldn't stap up antagonists the way you would a PC... It's a lot more work that isn't really going to improve your game. There's a couple of Scion Antagonists example starting at page 297 of Hero - one of Divus Iulius and one of Anansi - that would be a good starting point.<br /> In fact, checking that right now, there's a whole section on handling exactly that!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We can hear you saying it now: \u201cHold on, there\u2019s an entire book before this section that tells you how to<br /> make a Scion!\u201d And you\u2019re right, there is! If you intend to keep an Antagonist Scion around and make them<br /> a major part of the story, using the Character Creation system to build them and the Advancement system<br /> to maintain and improve them is an entirely reasonable thing to do.<br /> But the Antagonist system can handle Scions, and it can handle them fairly easily. Knacks translate<br /> well to Qualities, and Boons translate well to Flairs (in the above example, Knacks and Boons have been<br /> italicized for clarity). Both obey the same rules as if a player character were using them, replacing Legend<br /> with Tension if needed. Imbued Tension is set aside and reclaimed with the effect\u2019s end, as usual. If a roll is<br /> called for, use the most appropriate pool, or default to the Desperation Pool if none fit.<br /> You\u2019ll note the addition of Callings and Purviews to the typical Antagonist sheet. Callings are included<br /> for Fatebinding and any other effects the Storyguide may wish to emulate. Purviews, meanwhile, may be<br /> used to create marvels as usual, replacing Tension for Legend.<br /> If you\u2019re using the Antagonist system to create a Scion, don\u2019t worry too much about trying to match up<br /> to expectations of a player-character Scion. From the players\u2019 perspective, you\u2019re rolling dice and making<br /> strange effects go off, just as usual. The goal is, after all, to make less work for the Storyguide. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23975-pxgentleman","name":"PXGentleman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T05:22:46-08:00","id":1431675,"title":"","content":"12. Origin to Hero Tier - So I need to upgrade my antagonist to Hero level now ( story reasons ). <b>What are extra steps to add from Origin character to make her Hero then? </b>The <b>SCCQR</b> would imply those steps: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Give Legend 1.</li> <li>Add 2 more Callings, to 3 in total. 1 Calling need to comes from God Patron.</li> <li>Assign 5 dots to Callings, minimum 1 for each Calling.</li> <li>Add Knacks - Heroic cost 1, Immortal cost 2 in Callings dots.</li> <li>Define 1 Legendary Title ( reflecting Visitation events ).</li> <li>Distribute 7 Birthrights dots.</li> <li>Gain Pantheon Purview and 1 of your Patron God Purviews.</li> <li>Pick 2 Boons from your Purviews.</li> </ol><br /> I'm getting it right? Not missing anything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-12-2021, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T07:33:29-08:00","id":1431686,"title":"","content":"If you're making an Antagonist Scion, you should really just use the Antagonist rules in the back of the book. For an Antagonist Scion, you'll mostly need:<br /> <br /> 1. Their Archetype<br /> 2. Snag some Qualities and Flairs<br /> 3. Maybe make notes of what their Relics do, broadly (this one gives Enhancement, this one gives the Darkness Purview)<br /> 4. To activate Marvels of their Purviews, spend Tension instead of Legend.<br /> <br /> Boom, done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T06:24:40-08:00","id":1435185,"title":"","content":"I strongly advise to read A Pain in the Dice - Guide to Scion Character Creation<br /> <br /> Q: Pre-Visitation Scions don't have Legend points to imbue or spend, so: if they get a Purview by Guide or Relic means, how do they use it? Do they get the innate power?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1djeav1YTEwQq1fkDtWEKh7PPVFmzj3y-\" target=\"_blank\">The Repository</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13158-sir-bardiel","name":"Sir Bardiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13158_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T06:49:31-08:00","id":1435186,"title":"","content":"At best, I'd say they get the innate power, but I'd probably say they don't get anything. Birthrights are tied to a character's Legend, and Origin characters don't have a Legend yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T07:21:50-08:00","id":1435189,"title":"","content":"I would say - They can use how the story unfolds, seeing how it's all powered by Fate. So, Storyguide discretion, really. When they get Legend, it's players decision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T07:43:29-08:00","id":1435192,"title":"","content":"Birthrights are not tied to character legend. At least to the legend dots. An origin character can have birthright dots since char gen.<br /> <br /> If it was up to me, I would give access to the innate powers, as they are free, but notice that some innate powers are useless for example the ones that allow you to imbue legend instead of spending to gain scale.<br /> <br /> it would be really interesting story, for example a shield that make you shine, or an guide that teach you how to see and talk to dead people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T07:48:00-08:00","id":1435194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421956-character-creation-scion-2e?p=1435192#post1435192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Birthrights are not tied to character legend. At least to the legend dots. An origin character can have birthright dots since char gen.<br /> <br /> If it was up to me, I would give access to the innate powers, as they are free, but notice that some innate powers are useless for example the ones that allow you to imbue legend instead of spending to gain scale.<br /> <br /> it would be really interesting story, for example a center that make you shine, or an guide that teach you how to see and talk to dead people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I can see fluff-wise how it could be cool, I'm wondering if it's stated with a decent degree of disambiguation anywhere","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1djeav1YTEwQq1fkDtWEKh7PPVFmzj3y-\" target=\"_blank\">The Repository</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13158-sir-bardiel","name":"Sir Bardiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13158_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T07:55:26-08:00","id":1435196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421956-character-creation-scion-2e?p=1435192#post1435192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Birthrights are not tied to character legend. At least to the legend dots. An origin character can have birthright dots since char gen.</div> </div> </div> </div>From Hero p.201: &quot;When the Visitation occurs, many Gods grant their children Birthrights, powerful tokens of their esteem that become tied to the Scion\u2019s Legend.&quot; It's up to your own interpretation as to what that means, but they do use the phrase.<br /> <br /> Also, there are no Birthrights in the Origin character creation process. If the SG wants to give the characters Birthrights, that's up to the SG, but RAW, they don't get Birthrights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T08:27:13-08:00","id":1435202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421956-character-creation-scion-2e?p=1435196#post1435196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, there are no Birthrights in the Origin character creation process. If the SG wants to give the characters Birthrights, that's up to the SG, but RAW, they don't get Birthrights.</div> </div> </div> </div>Origin, p. 98: &quot;Each player character receives five extra Skill dots, an extra Attribute dot, and either two additional Knacks or four points of Birthrights (see Scion: Hero p. 201) at character creation.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T08:28:27-08:00","id":1435203,"title":"","content":"Origin p.98<br /> \u201cEach player character receives five extra Skill dots, an extra Attribute dot, and either two additional Knacks or four points of Birthrights (see Scion: Hero p. 201) at character creation.\u201d<br /> <br /> Edit: Geoffrey was faster... but he replied while I was copping, so I didn\u2019t saw his post until after I posted...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T08:33:07-08:00","id":1435204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sir Bardiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421956-character-creation-scion-2e?p=1435194#post1435194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes I can see fluff-wise how it could be cool, I'm wondering if it's stated with a decent degree of disambiguation anywhere</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing in the books. The only reference I can recall was one dev answering in the forum with something like: Origin characters get no purviews from birthrights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T08:48:34-08:00","id":1435205,"title":"","content":"Wow, I missed that. I would still say, though, the best you could do is get the innate power since you have no Legend to power anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T09:13:26-08:00","id":1435207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421956-character-creation-scion-2e?p=1435205#post1435205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, I missed that. I would still say, though, the best you could do is get the innate power since you have no Legend to power anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's the way I'd go, too. I don't see much wrong with an Origin-level character having a ring that makes them immune to fire or a belt that makes them stronger than normal. They can grow into the other powers later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T10:31:58-08:00","id":1435215,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'd probably let an Origin character use the innate ability of a Purview if it didn't require imbuing Legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my RPG podcast: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told</a><br /> Follow my ongoing Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"https://thefallofjiara.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log\" target=\"_blank\">The Fall of Jiara</a><br /> Check out my Community Content: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Chazz%20Kellner\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....hazz%20Kellner</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker","name":"ElfSpeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar702_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T10:43:23-08:00","id":1435221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421956-character-creation-scion-2e?p=1435204#post1435204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing in the books. The only reference I can recall was one dev answering in the forum with something like: Origin characters get no purviews from birthrights.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be weird, since it's stated in Origin creation chapter<br /> Could we @ a dev on this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1djeav1YTEwQq1fkDtWEKh7PPVFmzj3y-\" target=\"_blank\">The Repository</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13158-sir-bardiel","name":"Sir Bardiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13158_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T11:23:27-08:00","id":1435228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sir Bardiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421956-character-creation-scion-2e?p=1435221#post1435221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That'd be weird, since it's stated in Origin creation chapter<br /> Could we @ a dev on this?</div> </div> </div> </div>A birthright can grant knacks, stunts and situational enhancements, what is not available to regular people, that\u2019s what a birthright could do at origin level. My origin character, for example, had a magical sword that had a lot of enhancements and the motif \u201ccan cut anything\u201d, but gave no other effects, at least until he become quero and gained a purview (Journey in the case, because he could open portals to other places by cutting reality open).<br /> <br /> I still think that the innate power of the purview would be available to an origin level character, as well as any other power as long the character can use a sacrifice to gain one point of legend and spend it immediately. For example, a staff that allows to see the dead could be used in a ceremony (an specific sacrifice) to cast a Death Marvel. That would give the item a importance in the game and to a cult that works around it, for example a cult leader that can summon spirits, or a artisan that have a magical hammer that allow him to do offers to the gods to create powerful items.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T12:19:55-08:00","id":1435235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421956-character-creation-scion-2e?p=1435228#post1435228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A birthright can grant knacks, stunts and situational enhancements, what is not available to regular people, that\u2019s what a birthright could do at origin level. My origin character, for example, had a magical sword that had a lot of enhancements and the motif \u201ccan cut anything\u201d, but gave no other effects, at least until he become quero and gained a purview (Journey in the case, because he could open portals to other places by cutting reality open).<br /> <br /> I still think that the innate power of the purview would be available to an origin level character, as well as any other power as long the character can use a sacrifice to gain one point of legend and spend it immediately. For example, a staff that allows to see the dead could be used in a ceremony (an specific sacrifice) to cast a Death Marvel. That would give the item a importance in the game and to a cult that works around it, for example a cult leader that can summon spirits, or a artisan that have a magical hammer that allow him to do offers to the gods to create powerful items.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is really useful. I kind of forgot about the sacrifices, and I agree on everything","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1djeav1YTEwQq1fkDtWEKh7PPVFmzj3y-\" target=\"_blank\">The Repository</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13158-sir-bardiel","name":"Sir Bardiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13158_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T21:51:38-07:00","id":1457864,"title":"","content":"13. <b>How many Paths character can have?</b> Can it have more than basic 3 - Origin, Role and Pantheon?<br /> <br /> 14. <b>Can non-Denizen become Denizen - and by this, change it's Role Path to Denizen Path?</b> Skills dots, etc. stays on character like it was before then?<br /> <br /> 15. <b>Can character suddenly find new Path?</b> Like character uncover it was secretly Denizen, or Denizen-related, for 4th Path, for example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-28-2021, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T22:21:46-07:00","id":1457957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421956-character-creation-scion-2e?p=1457864#post1457864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">13. <b>How many Paths character can have?</b> Can it have more than basic 3 - Origin, Role and Pantheon?<br /> <br /> 14. <b>Can non-Denizen become Denizen - and by this, change it's Role Path to Denizen Path?</b> Skills dots, etc. stays on character like it was before then?<br /> <br /> 15. <b>Can character suddenly find new Path?</b> Like character uncover it was secretly Denizen, or Denizen-related, for 4th Path, for example?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't feel at all qualified to answer this but I'm doing it because no one else has.<br /> <br /> 13: I would probably not allow a player to have more paths, but I would allow them to change their paths as a part of roleplaying. Maybe a character starts with the Role Path &quot;Professional Assassin&quot; and later on starts to repent and feel guilty, then they change this path into something else. They gain no new skill dots but they have through roleplaying acquired a new network of contacts. Maybe their old Role Path then subsumes or is integrated into their Origin Path to represent how those old contacts and skills are still there.<br /> <br /> 14: Anything is possible with gods. I'm not sure if a Scion could become a Denizen, but if it is awesome enough I'd probably allow it on the condition that one of the Scion's old Callings is taken up by new Denizen Calling dots instead and Knacks are switched out to more appropriate ones where necessary. One thing you could do is allow the Pantheon Path to double as the new denizen path if your transformation into a Denizen is done by a god. For example if you have a Scion of Poseidon who is then transformed into a mermaid / merman then I would allow their Pantheon Path double as their Merfolk Path as well.<br /> <br /> 15: Again, I would not allow a 4th Path but would allow alterations of already existing Paths. The reason for this is because otherwise the character would have an extra +2 dice per session and also one more Path to draw on their contacts from one more Path than the other players which doesn't seem right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","user":"Aristarkos","date":". 08-29-2021, 01:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-29T06:01:25-07:00","id":1457964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421956-character-creation-scion-2e?p=1457864#post1457864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">13. <b>How many Paths character can have?</b> Can it have more than basic 3 - Origin, Role and Pantheon?<br /> <br /> 14. <b>Can non-Denizen become Denizen - and by this, change it's Role Path to Denizen Path?</b> Skills dots, etc. stays on character like it was before then?<br /> <br /> 15. <b>Can character suddenly find new Path?</b> Like character uncover it was secretly Denizen, or Denizen-related, for 4th Path, for example?</div> </div> </div> </div>13, You can add more Paths by making appropriate connections through play (Origin, p.95). It's recommended that you don't go beyond five of them.<br /> <br /> 14. I'd agree with Aristarkos: if a Scion takes on a Denizen Path <i>and</i> wants access to the Knacks associated with it, she would have to switch out one of her Callings to make room. Note that it's possible to have a Denizen Path without taking the Calling: if you want to be a satyr but don't want it to be a significant part of your identity, make it a Path, take the appropriate Persistent Condition, and don't change anything else.<br /> <br /> 15. Remember that a Path comes with several benefits in the form of connections, Twists of Fate, and a dice bonus. Unless there's a way to justify giving all of that to someone at once, it's probably better to make it a longer process to adopt a new one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}